## 1. System Overview

NullifyAI sits **between** an AI agent and any downstream system the agent would otherwise call directly. Every decision the agent attempts to execute is routed through the NullifyAI enforcement layer before it reaches the outside world.

```
  Without NullifyAI:
  ┌───────────┐        ┌──────────────────────┐
  │ AI Agent  │───────▶│ Downstream System     │
  └───────────┘        │ (EHR / LOS / Fraud DB)│
                       └──────────────────────┘

  With NullifyAI:
  ┌───────────┐   action()  ┌─────────────────┐  verdict  ┌──────────────────────┐
  │ AI Agent  │────────────▶│  NullifyAI SDK  │──────────▶│ Agent continues OR   │
  └───────────┘             │  (wrap, 1ms)    │           │ is blocked/escalated │
                            └────────┬────────┘           └──────────────────────┘
                                     │ POST /v1/evaluate
                                     ▼
                            ┌─────────────────────────────┐
                            │  Enforcement API (P95 <10ms) │
                            └─────────────────────────────┘
```

**Core guarantee:** every decision receives a verdict — `APPROVED`, `BLOCKED`, or `ESCALATED` — in under 10ms at the 95th percentile, with zero changes to the agent's source code.

