### 2.2 Enforcement Path — Decision Blocked

An agent attempts a decision that violates one or more active policies. NullifyAI returns `BLOCKED` and the agent is prevented from calling any downstream system.

```
Agent Code               SDK                   Enforcement API              Slack / PagerDuty
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
agent.action(payload)
    │                                           [+4ms] Policy Engine
    │                                           Rule HC-001: formulary_success_rate < 0.95
    │                                           ──── VIOLATION ────
    │                                           Rule stopped; remaining rules skipped
    │                                           │
    │                                           [+3ms] Drift Detector
    │                                           Drift score: 87  (Severe, >80)
    │                                           │
    │                                           [+2ms] Verdict Engine
    │                                           verdict: BLOCKED
    │                                           reason: "HC-001 formulary_rate=0.78 < 0.95"
    │                                           exposure_estimate: $31,000
    │                                           │
    │◀─────────────────────────────────────── 200 OK { verdict: "BLOCKED", rule: "HC-001" }
    │                                           │
    ▼                                           [async] Alert Dispatcher
nullify.wrap() throws                           │── POST Slack #compliance-alerts
  NullifyBlockedError                           │── PagerDuty L2 incident (drift >80)
    │                                           │── Write audit record (signed)
    ▼
Agent catches error
Agent does NOT call downstream system
Agent may: notify user, log, retry with
  different parameters, or halt
```

**Key property:** the downstream system (EHR, LOS, Fraud DB) is never called. The damage is prevented, not just logged.

