### 2.3 Escalation Path — Human Review Required

A decision cannot be auto-approved or auto-blocked — it requires a human analyst to review before execution proceeds.

```
Agent Code               SDK                   Enforcement API              Analyst Dashboard
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
agent.action(payload)
    │                                           Policy Engine:
    │                                           Rule F-09: high_value_claim > $50,000
    │                                           Threshold: escalate, do not block
    │                                           │
    │                                           Verdict Engine:
    │                                           verdict: ESCALATED
    │                                           escalation_queue: "claims-review"
    │                                           sla_minutes: 30
    │
    │◀─────────────────────────────────────── 200 OK { verdict: "ESCALATED" }
    │
    ▼
Agent suspends execution
Places decision in pending queue
Returns "pending review" to end user
    │
    │                                           [async]
    │                                           ──── Analyst notified (Slack + email)
    │                                           ──── Decision visible in Review Queue UI
    │
    │                               ◀──── Analyst opens Dashboard
    │                               ◀──── Reviews decision details + audit context
    │                               ◀──── Clicks APPROVE or REJECT
    │
    │◀─────────────────────────────────────── Webhook: { decision_id, outcome: "approved" }
    │
    ▼
Agent resumes
If approved → calls downstream system
If rejected → halts, logs, notifies end user
```

