### 2.5 Onboarding Flow — Operator Sets Up an Agent

How a new enterprise customer goes from zero to first intercepted decision.

```
Operator                  NullifyAI Portal         SDK / CI               Production
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. Sign up / log in
   │
   ▼
2. Create Agent Profile
   Agent name, vertical, baseline period (default: 7 days)
   └──▶ API returns: agent_id, api_key
   │
   ▼
3. Select Policy Template
   Choose vertical: Healthcare / Lending / Fraud
   Enable shadow mode (optional — evaluate but don't block)
   └──▶ Policy set saved; rules activated
   │
   ▼
4. Install SDK
   pip install nullify-sdk   or   npm install @nullify/sdk
   │
   ▼
5. Wrap Agent (1 line of code)
   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │  from nullify import wrap                              │
   │  agent = wrap(my_agent, api_key="...", agent_id="...") │
   └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   │
   ▼
6. Deploy to staging → run smoke tests
   SDK fires test decision → enforcement API responds
   Dashboard shows first intercepted decision ✓
   │
   ▼
7. Disable shadow mode → enforcement goes live
   First BLOCKED or APPROVED verdict in production
   Baseline period begins (7 days before drift scoring activates)
   │
   ▼
Target: contract signed → first live interception < 4 hours
```

