### 3.2 Enforcement Pipeline — Internal Layers

Each incoming decision passes through four layers in series. Every layer has an independent timeout; a layer timeout triggers the circuit breaker (fail-open or fail-closed, per agent config).

| Layer | Component | Responsibility | P95 Budget | Timeout |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Intercept Layer** | Deserialize payload; attach agent metadata; validate API key | 1ms | 5ms |
| 2 | **Policy Engine** | Evaluate all active rules in parallel; return first violation or all-clear | 4ms | 8ms |
| 3 | **Drift Detector** | CUSUM score vs 7-day EWMA baseline; classify threshold tier | 3ms | 6ms |
| 4 | **Verdict Engine** | Compose final verdict; sign with HMAC-SHA256; build audit record | 2ms | 4ms |
| 5 | **Audit Logger** | Async write to S3 + DynamoDB; trigger alert dispatcher if needed | async | 50ms |

**Circuit breaker behavior:**
- If Enforcement API is unreachable: SDK uses local rule cache (subset of high-priority rules).
- If local cache also unavailable: agent proceeds based on per-agent `on_failure` config — either `fail_open` (APPROVED) or `fail_closed` (BLOCKED).
- Every circuit-breaker event is logged and triggers a Slack/PagerDuty alert.

