## 6. Latency Budget

The P95 <10ms guarantee breaks down as follows across the four synchronous layers:

```
 ms  0        2        4        6        8       10
     │        │        │        │        │        │
     ├────────┤────────────────────────────────────
     │  1ms   │  Intercept Layer (deserialize, auth)
     │        ├──────────────────────────────────
     │        │     4ms    │  Policy Engine (50+ rules, parallel)
     │        │            ├─────────────────────
     │        │            │   3ms   │  Drift Detector (CUSUM score)
     │        │            │         ├────────────
     │        │            │         │  2ms  │  Verdict Engine (compose + sign)
     │        │            │         │       ├──
     ├────────┴────────────┴─────────┴───────┤ ~10ms total (P95)
                                              │
                                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
                                   5. Audit Logger (async, does not
                                      block the synchronous response)
                                      Target: <50ms write to S3 + DDB
```

| Percentile | Target | Breach Threshold | SLA |
|---|---|---|---|
| P50 | <4ms | — | — |
| P95 | <10ms | >20ms alert | >30ms SLA breach |
| P99 | <25ms | >50ms alert | >75ms SLA breach |

Measured via Datadog APM on the `/v1/evaluate` endpoint at sustained 500 concurrent decisions/second load.

